data
  title Saturation signal: load average vs PSI
  desc Why PSI (kernel 4.20+) replaces the load-average proxy
  compares
    - label Load average
      children
        - label Mixes task states
          desc Runnable + uninterruptible conflated
        - label Skews with core count
          desc Load 10: fine on 64 cores, dire on 2
        - label 1-min average hides spikes
          desc A transient 5s crunch barely registers
        - label Threshold is guesswork
          desc No clean alert rule across host sizes
    - label PSI · kernel 4.20+
      children
        - label Wall-clock stall time
          desc Percent of time tasks waited on a resource
        - label Core-count independent
          desc Same meaning on 2 or 64 cores
        - label some vs full signal
          desc full = every non-idle task stalled
        - label Alertable, sub-1% overhead
          desc K8s 1.27+ uses it for eviction
